evo's patch for michi-c2 (github.com/db3108/michi-c2, commit d2a4cb8), so it
can play as a tournament and benchmark opponent:

- expand() allocates one tree child per candidate move plus the NULL
  terminator, then may append a pass child over the terminator; most_urgent()
  then reads past the array (a crash after an opponent's pass with few legal
  moves). Allocate room for both.
- FORALL_NEIGHBORS and FORALL_DIAGONAL_NEIGHBORS read delta[4] and delta[8]
  after their last iteration; delta[8] is past the array.
- The GTP play command accepts a move that repeats an earlier position: evo
  and its arena forbid only a simple ko retake, and michi answered such a move
  with "? ... Positional Superko rule violation". michi's own genmove still
  avoids repeating a position.
- Portable Makefile: no -march=native or -msse4, cc instead of gcc, and
  -fcommon for the globals that several files define; no x86intrin.h (only
  compiler builtins are used).
- Options after the mode: --sims N, --seed N (0 is a fixed seed, not the
  clock), --play-until-end.
- time_settings and time_left are accepted and ignored, so the playouts per
  move stay N_SIMS and the moves do not depend on the clock.
- verbosity 0 by default (2 printed the board to stderr after every command),
  the log goes to /dev/null instead of michi.log, and no large pattern files
  are loaded from the working directory.
- The move history holds 10,000 moves (passes included) instead of 1,083;
  once it is full, play and genmove answer "? Error - move history full"
  instead of writing past the arrays.

